# GeoClue -- the D-Bus location service. gnome-control-center's Privacy ->
# Location panel is a front end to it, and gnome-shell's location indicator
# talks to it directly.
#
# BLFS 12.4, pinned here rather than in versions.env: versions.env is
# regenerated wholesale from the LFS book by tools/pin-versions.sh, so a desktop
# pin placed there is destroyed by the next `make pin`.
SRC_URL=https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/geoclue/geoclue/-/archive/2.7.2/geoclue-2.7.2.tar.bz2
SRC_SHA256=01d24a44a036769049411899ae83c9a86f73d272cca3df6af5a03bfac32456d2
SRC_DIR=geoclue-2.7.2

# LIKE ITS NEIGHBOUR, EVERY OPTION HERE IS A BOOLEAN DEFAULTING TRUE. Doing
# nothing turns all of it on, including two things that cannot work here and one
# that would be acquired without a decision.
#
# -Dnmea-source=false. Defaults TRUE and needs avahi-client AND avahi-glib
# (src/meson.build:56), neither of which is packaged. Network NMEA -- reading a
# GPS shared over the LAN by another machine -- is the feature lost, and it is
# lost to a missing package rather than to a preference.
#
# -Dvapi=false. Defaults TRUE; vala is not packaged.
#
# -Dgtk-doc=false. Defaults TRUE; gtk-doc is not packaged. (Its description in
# meson_options.txt says "for Geocode-GLib", copy-pasted from the other project
# -- do not read that as evidence about anything.)
#
# -Ddemo-agent=false. Defaults TRUE and pulls libnotify (demo/meson.build:38),
# which IS packaged, so the default would quietly acquire that edge for a demo
# program. The real agent on this desktop is gnome-shell's, which implements the
# Agent interface itself.
#
# THE THREE MODEM SOURCES ARE ENABLED DELIBERATELY, and that is a decision
# rather than an inheritance. -D3g-source, -Dcdma-source and -Dmodem-gps-source
# all default TRUE and each pulls mm-glib (src/meson.build:36) -- and
# ModemManager IS packaged here, in NETWORK_PKGS, which precedes this group. So
# leaving them alone would acquire a real cross-tier dependency by doing
# nothing, which is exactly the shape this tree keeps getting caught by. They
# are stated, and ModemManager is declared, because a laptop with a WWAN card
# has no other way to report a position: without them geoclue on this desktop
# can only fall back to network-based lookup.
#
# -Dcompass=true is stated for completeness and costs nothing: it reads headings
# from net.hadess.SensorProxy over D-Bus, which is an interface rather than a
# build dependency -- there is no package behind it to find.
#
# NOT PINNED, BECAUSE IT CANNOT BE, AND THE OUTCOME IS ASSERTED INSTEAD:
# -Dsystemd-system-unit-dir is a `type: 'string'` option with NO value at all,
# which in these files means "go and find it" rather than "no" (the NetworkManager
# and ModemManager trap). data/meson.build:57-63 falls back to
# `dependency('systemd', required: false)` and installs geoclue.service only if
# that is found. elogind provides libelogind.pc and the libsystemd.pc alias but
# NOT systemd.pc, so it FAILS CLOSED here -- the right outcome, arrived at by
# accident rather than by instruction. There is no value that means "never", so
# install.sh asserts the unit is absent; that is what converts an accident into
# a guarantee.
#
# -Ddbus-sys-dir is the same shape and benign: empty falls back to
# $datadir/dbus-1/system.d, a computed path rather than a probe of the build
# machine, so it is deterministic. Left alone, and the file is asserted where
# that computation puts it.
MESON_ARGS="-Dlibgeoclue=true \
-Dintrospection=true \
-Dvapi=false \
-Dgtk-doc=false \
-Denable-backend=true \
-Ddemo-agent=false \
-Dnmea-source=false \
-D3g-source=true -Dcdma-source=true -Dmodem-gps-source=true \
-Dcompass=true"
